// entity 8 -- the press indicator, authored on the dynamic tier. switch-demo.ts
// holds it dark on spawn and fades it up on press, so it is the confirmation a
// tester sees when the switch fires.
// Sits 24 units off the switch plate face at y 312, centred on it in x and z,
// so the confirmation lands where a tester is already looking. Activation has
// no facing check, so the press can happen while looking away -- that is
// exactly why the indicator has to be readable at the console rather than
// somewhere else in the room.
// The 24 units are a shadow budget, not an arbitrary gap -- do not close it. A
// dynamic point light is eligible for the cube shadow pool and casts a real
// WORLD shadow off static brushwork; _cast_entity_shadows only suppresses
// moving-entity occluders, and there is no KVP that disables the world shadow.
// The plate stands 8 units proud of the wall, so a light d units in front of it
// throws the plate's silhouette onto the wall magnified (d + 8) / d. At d = 8
// that is 2x: a 48 x 32 plate casts a 96 x 64 shadow, framing the panel in a
// 24-unit dark border that switches on with the press. At d = 24 it is 1.33x
// and reads as falloff. Pull the light toward the plate and the halo comes
// back.
// Deliberately the brightest light in the map (400 against the room lights' 100
// and 200) and deliberately NOT dim. An earlier pass authored it dim and
// short-range on the theory that a console indicator should read as local
// detail; in-engine it was then invisible against the room lighting, which
// defeats the whole point of the fixture. Brightness is what makes a press
// unmistakable; proximity to the plate is what makes it mean "this switch".
// Keep both -- trading either one back costs the check this map exists for.
// light_dynamic is a design decision, not a spelling of light. A baked light
// that a script animates leaves the static lightmap for the animated-lightmap
// atlas, and animated weight maps only cover atlas array layer 0 -- a face the
// packer spills onto a higher layer is dark before AND after the press, with no
// assert and no warning. Coarsening _lightmap_density does not help: the layer
// dimension shrinks along with the texel count, so the layer count never
// reaches 1. A dynamic light bakes into nothing, so it has no atlas and no
// layer to spill past -- it is evaluated live in the forward direct loop and
// shadowed from the runtime pool. Price paid: this light contributes no baked
// indirect bounce, which a press indicator does not need.
// The dynamic class omits every bake KVP -- style, _bake_only, _shadow_type,
// _animated, _start_inactive -- because nothing on this tier bakes. The tier
// comes from the classname; there is no KVP that selects it.
// _cast_entity_shadows 0 drops the per-entity occluder pass for this light --
// nothing in this fixture moves through its range that needs to cast onto the
// world. The light's WORLD shadow is unaffected; that rides the tier itself,
// not this toggle.
{
"classname" "light_dynamic"
"origin" "224 288 56"
"light" "400"
"_color" "80 255 140"
"_falloff_range" "133"
"delay" "0"
"_cast_entity_shadows" "0"
"_tags" "switch_demo_console_light"
}
